 "fill_reason": {
  "pin_bound": "routing/perimeter-bound, not area: macros block M1-M4 (cap M5) so the outline is set by a >= 420 um macro-free W<->E band at every x (xg5: 121 um at the ROM column -> GPL routability failure) and 11,914 face pins (W/E 2,554 each, N ~3.76k, S ~3.05k); 648.0 x 864.0: 37 macros 115.8k + std ~30k = ~26% util; pins 11,914 on full faces"
 },
 "structural_change": "S81-XG5FP (10-21, LEAD-S81): STRUCTURAL floorplan successor of s81sl_xg5 after both xg5/xg5k routes crashed at\n3_5 DPL-0038 (util 121%): 3_3 GPL routability never converged (36-47% of gcells overflowed, weighted congestion 1.6-2.0,\n8 inflation rounds), then repair_design inserted 965k buffers for 231k slew violations.\nCause: the 37 macros obstruct M1-M4 and the tile routes M2-M5, so NO horizontal (M2/M4) wire can cross a macro. The xg5\nplan stacked 8 SRAMs per bank column (y 108-437) and all 7 ROMs in one column (y 64.8-505.6 = 441 of 561.6 um): at the\nROM column only 121 um of height is free for W<->E wires (~1.4k M2+M4 tracks) while the ring needs ri_w->ro_e +\nri_e->ro_w (2 x 1,104 b) + nx (346 b) + the 3,072-b gather port + 6,144 SRAM read bits across it.  SRAM pin faces\n(W/E, 412 pins on 41 um = 10/um, 3.3k per 8-stack face) face 34.8-43 um channels, the W one shared with 2,554 tile pins.\nFix (xg5fb): no column stacks more than 4 SRAMs (164 um) or 2+2 ROMs; every column is split into a S stack and a N\nstack with a full-width macro-free centre band, so >= 420 um of height is free for W<->E routing at every x, and\n8-stack pin faces become 4-stack faces (1.65k pins) (xg5 channels, half the pins per face); W pin face no longer abuts an SRAM face.\nfb: 648 x 864 (same x columns as xg5: banks 43.2 / 216 / 432, ROM 345.6, exp 561.6); mac 0-3 S y 86.4, mac 4-7 N\ny 611.28; ROMs 3 S (y 86.4) + 4 N (y 524.88); exp SRAMs 3 S + 3 N.\nRTL, pins (faces/order), clock K=16, census fixes = xg5c e1c24fa0a unchanged.\n\nPrevious:\nS81-TILES-E (10-20, LEAD9-S81 decision 14:30): kit s81sl_xg5 = the slice gather sub-leaf re-merged (ot_s81sl_xg5 =\not_s81sl_rs + ot_s81sl_xs4 + issuer relay) so the 3 x 1,031-b gather port stays inside one tile.\n\nWhy: the split rs4 leaf was PIN-BOUND (13,750 signal pins in 864 x 518.4, util 2.6%; at <= 6 pins/um its minimum outline\ngives ~3.7%) and its placement TT was -313.8 ps; owner 10-20 09:09 REPARTITION rule for pin-bound tiles.\nOutline = the original xg slot 648 x 561.6 (base spec base_s81sl_xg_spec_xg1019.json, claude/s81-xg-1019): estimated\nstd ~30k um2 (rs4 synth 12.3k + xs4 synth 16.5k + XG5 copies) + 37 macros 115.8k um2 = 146k -> util ~40%; pins\n11,914 on full faces <= 5.8/um (W/E 4.5, N 5.8, S 4.7).\nMacro map (SRAM / ROM / exp-SRAM pins are on the L/R faces only -> deliberate N-S abutted stacks, gap 0.024 um, bare\ntouching faces; channels only between columns; stack origins on the 43.2 / 21.6 grid, as the original xg kit):\n  x 43.2   bank 1 (W ring source) 8 x 128x256 SRAM, y 108 + 41.088 k   | x 216.0 bank 0 (own) | x 432.0 bank 2 (E source)\n  x 345.6  7 x ROM 4096x72, y 64.8 + 62.976 k\n  x 561.6  6 x exponent SRAM 128x64 (source 0/1/2 x beat bit 2), y 108 + 27.6 k\nChannels: 34.8-78 um between macro columns, W edge 43.2, E edge 52.7, S strip 108 / N strip 108 for the face pin cells.\n\nXG5c (DRIVE-S81-XG 10-20): xg5b gate PRE_GATE_NATIVE_CENSUS_REFUSED, 3 roots > 32 in ot_s81sl_xs4_cal: pok[2] (base_q 12 + nrows 13 enables, 36 mapped), due[4] (last_ts 24-b mux + age/act/rpt, 57), due5 (consume_index 13 + count/fault/fetch, 37). Fix: pq 4 -> 6 kept copies (pok[4] nrows, pok[5] consume_index); kept due instances u_due5c (consume_index) and u_due4l0/u_due4l1 (last_ts 12 b each). Value-preserving (same function per copy).",
